      "text": "To convert from spherical coordinates \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi)\\) to rectangular coordinates \\((x, y, z)\\), we use the following formulas:\n\\[ x = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta, \\]\n\\[ y = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta, \\]\n\\[ z = \\rho \\cos \\phi. \\]\n\nGiven spherical coordinates \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)\\), we can substitute \\(\\rho = 3\\), \\(\\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\), and \\(\\phi = 0\\) into the formulas.\n\nFirst, calculate \\(x\\):\n\\[ x = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta = 3 \\sin 0 \\cos \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}. \\]\nSince \\(\\sin 0 = 0\\), we have:\n\\[ x = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 0. \\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(y\\):\n\\[ y = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta = 3 \\sin 0 \\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 0. \\]\n\nFinally, calculate \\(z\\):\n\\[ z = \\rho \\cos \\phi = 3 \\cos 0 = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3. \\]\n\nThus, the rectangular coordinates are \\((x, y, z) = (0, 0, 3)\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
